                     (30.4% identity in 464 aa overlap); etc. BELONGS TO THE
                     PYRIDINE NUCLEOTIDE-DISULFIDE OXIDOREDUCTASES CLASS-I.
                     COFACTOR: FAD (BY SIMILARITY).
                     REMARK-M.bovis-M.tuberculosis: In Mycobacterium bovis,
