                     of the Mycobacterium tuberculosis PPE family, similar to
                     many e.g. O06246|Rv3429|MTCY77.01 (178 aa), FASTA scores:
                     opt: 781, E(): 7e-44, (69.9% identity in 176 aa overlap);
                     and downstream Q50702|YY26_MYCTU|Rv3426|MTCY78.03c (232
                     aa), FASTA scores: opt: 517, E(): 1.2e-26, (68.0% identity
                     in 125 aa overlap); MTV049_11, MTCY428_16, MTV049_22,
                     MTV049_30, MTCY261_4; etc. Rv3429: Member of the M.
                     tuberculosis PPE family, similar to many e.g. the upstream
                     Q50703|YY25_MYCTU|Rv3425|MTCY78.04c (176 aa), FASTA
                     scores: opt: 781, E(): 1.9e-44, (69.9% identity in 176 aa
                     overlap); and Q50702|YY26_MYCTU|Rv3426|MTCY78.03c (232
                     aa), FASTA scores: opt: 555, E(): 1.7e-29, (72.0% identity
                     in 125 aa overlap) (but diverges at 3' end)); etc.
                     REMARK-M.bovis-M.tuberculosis: In Mycobacterium bovis, a
                     large deletion of 4926 bp (RD6) leads to the loss of the
                     COOH part of PPE57, and the following CDSs, PPE58,
                     Rv3427c, Rv3428c and PPE59 compared to Mycobacterium
                     tuberculosis strain H37Rv. Mb3459 found to be expressed
                     during exponential growth in Sauton's minimal media by
                     RNA-sequencing."
