                     /note="Mb3556, -, len: 386 aa. Equivalent to Rv3526, len:
                     386 aa, from Mycobacterium tuberculosis strain H37Rv,
                     (100.0% identity in 386 aa overlap). Hypothetical
                     oxidoreductase (EC 1.-.-.-), highly similar, except in
                     C-terminus (also longer 69 aa), to O69348|ORF12 PROTEIN
                     (function unknown) from Rhodococcus erythropolis (316 aa)
                     FASTA scores: opt: 1137, E(): 6.9e-65, (59.6% identity in
                     250 aa overlap). Also some similarity with several
                     aminopyrrolnitrin oxidases (PRND proteins, involved in the
                     pathway for pyrrolnitrin biosynthesis, a secondary
                     metabolite derived from tryptophan which has strong
                     anti-fungal activity) e.g. Q9RPG0|PRND from Myxococcus
                     fulvus (379 aa), FASTA scores: opt: 322, E(): 4.4e-13,
                     (25.85% identity in 352 aa overlap); Q9RPG4|PRND from
                     Burkholderia cepacia (Pseudomonas cepacia) (373 aa) FASTA
                     scores: opt: 306, E(): 4.5e-12, (25.2% identity in 373 aa
                     overlap); P95483|PRND from Pseudomonas fluorescens (363
                     aa), FASTA scores: opt: 305, E(): 5.1e-12, (25.0% identity
                     in 372 aa overlap); etc. And also some similarity to other
                     putative enzymes like dioxygenases, oxidases, vanillate
                     O-demethyl oxygenase, etc. Protein product from Mb3556
                     detected using SWATH mass spectrometry. Mb3556 found to be
                     expressed during exponential growth in Sauton's minimal
                     media by RNA-sequencing."
