     CDS             4116745..4119942
                     /locus_tag="BQ2027_MB3755"
                     /note="Mb3755, -, len: 1065 aa. Equivalent to Rv3728, len:
                     1065 aa, from Mycobacterium tuberculosis strain H37Rv,
                     (99.9% identity in 1065 aa overlap). Probable conserved
                     transmembrane protein organised into two domains. Domain
                     comprising the first ~510 aa residues is similar to
                     various multidrug resistance and efflux proteins and
                     contains sugar transport protein signature 1 (PS00216).
                     Domain corresponding to the last 550 aa residues contains
                     cyclic nucleotide-binding domain signature 2 (PS00889) and
                     is very similar to
                     Q50733|YP65_MYCTU|Rv2565|MT2641|MTCY9C4.03c hypothetical
                     62.1 kDa protein from Mycobacterium tuberculosis (31.0%
                     identity in 546 aa overlap). Highly similar to
                     O05884|Rv3239c|MTCY20B11.14c PROBABLE TRANSMEMBRANE
                     TRANSPORT PROTEIN from Mycobacterium tuberculosis (1048
                     aa) FASTA scores: opt: 4328, E(): 5e-201, (64.15% identity
                     in 1046 aa overlap). N-terminal end similar to
                     P71879|Rv2333c|MTCY3G12.01|MTCY98.02c (537 aa);
                     P71836|Rv0783c|MTCY369.27c (540 aa); and
                     O07753|Rv1877|MTCY180.41c (687 aa). SEEMS BELONG TO THE
                     SUGAR TRANSPORTER FAMILY. Possibly member of major
                     facilitator superfamily (MFS). Mb3755 found to be
                     expressed during exponential growth in Sauton's minimal
                     media by RNA-sequencing."
