                     strain H37Rv, (99.8% identity in 637 aa overlap). Probable
                     fadD32, fatty-acid-CoA synthetase (EC 6.2.1.-), equivalent
                     to Q9CDB2|FADD32|ML0100 PUTATIVE ACYL-COA SYNTHETASE from
                     Mycobacterium leprae (635 aa), FASTA scores: opt: 3892,
                     E(): 0, (93.05% identity in 632 aa overlap); and highly
                     similar to others from Mycobacterium leprae. Also similar
                     to others from Mycobacterium tuberculosis e.g.
                     P95288|FADD31|Rv1925|MTCY09F9.39c (620 aa), FASTA scores:
                     opt: 1567, E(): 1.7e-88, (47.05% identity in 612 aa
                     overlap); MTCY338_18, MTCY349_40, MTV005_21, MTCY24G1_8,
                     MTCY19G5_7, MTCY4D9_17; and MBU75685_1 ACYL-COA LIGASE
                     from Mycobacterium bovis. Protein product from Mb3831c
                     detected using shotgun mass spectrometry and SWATH mass
                     spectrometry. Mb3831c found to be expressed during
                     exponential growth in Sauton's minimal media by
                     RNA-sequencing."
